template-size: TPM2B_TEMPLATE is bounded by the unpadded sizeof(TPMT_PUBLIC)

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Part 2, Table "Definition of TPM2B_TEMPLATE
Structure"): "buffer[size]{:sizeof(TPMT_PUBLIC)}", and Part 2, "Data
Alignment": "When used in a table to indicate a maximum size, the sizeof()
function returns the octet-aligned size of the structure, with no padding."

The reference bounds TPM2B_TEMPLATE with the C sizeof(TPMT_PUBLIC), which
includes the alignment padding of TPMA_OBJECT and of the UINT32 exponent of
TPMS_RSA_PARMS: 356 bytes instead of 350 with this profile, so templates of
351 to 356 bytes are accepted instead of TPM_RC_SIZE. The bound is the
unpadded size (the same kind of padding issue as bug-fix-tpmu-name-size).
Found by differential fuzzing.
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/support/Marshal.c b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/support/Marshal.c
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/support/Marshal.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/support/Marshal.c
@@ -5250,12 +5250,31 @@
 }
 
 // Table "Definition of TPM2B_TEMPLATE Structure" (Part 2: Structures)
+// tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+// TPM2B_TEMPLATE is bounded by "sizeof(TPMT_PUBLIC)", which Part 2 ("Data
+// Alignment") defines as "the octet-aligned size of the structure, with no
+// padding", not the padded C sizeof. The largest TPMU_PUBLIC_PARMS members
+// are TPMS_RSA_PARMS (unpadded: symmetric, scheme, keyBits, exponent) and
+// TPMS_ECC_PARMS (no padding of its own); TPM2B_DIGEST and TPMU_PUBLIC_ID
+// have no padding of their own.
+#define TPMS_RSA_PARMS_PACKED_SIZE                                        \
+    (sizeof(TPMT_SYM_DEF_OBJECT) + sizeof(TPMT_RSA_SCHEME) + sizeof(UINT16) \
+     + sizeof(UINT32))
+#define TPMU_PUBLIC_PARMS_PACKED_SIZE                                \
+    (TPMS_RSA_PARMS_PACKED_SIZE > sizeof(TPMS_ECC_PARMS)               \
+         ? TPMS_RSA_PARMS_PACKED_SIZE                                  \
+         : sizeof(TPMS_ECC_PARMS))
+#define TPMT_PUBLIC_PACKED_SIZE                                         \
+    (sizeof(TPMI_ALG_PUBLIC) + sizeof(TPMI_ALG_HASH) + sizeof(UINT32) \
+     + sizeof(TPM2B_DIGEST) + TPMU_PUBLIC_PARMS_PACKED_SIZE      \
+     + sizeof(TPMU_PUBLIC_ID))
+
 TPM_RC
 TPM2B_TEMPLATE_Unmarshal(TPM2B_TEMPLATE* target, BYTE** buffer, INT32* size)
 {
     TPM_RC result;
     result = UINT16_Unmarshal((UINT16*)&(target->t.size), buffer, size);
-    if((result == TPM_RC_SUCCESS) && (target->t.size > sizeof(TPMT_PUBLIC)))
+    if((result == TPM_RC_SUCCESS) && (target->t.size > TPMT_PUBLIC_PACKED_SIZE))
         result = TPM_RC_SIZE;
